  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Pour 1 1/2 cups of water into a pot, add the quinoa and bring to the boil. Cover, reduce the heat and cook for 15 minutes. Transfer to a bowl, add the finely chopped onion, grated carrot, grated and well-squeezed zucchini, eggs, rice flour and olive oil, then season with salt and pepper."
    },
    {
      "text": "With damp hands, shape the mixture into 20 firmly packed, flattened patties (pressing firmly stops them falling apart)."
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the canola oil in a large non-stick pan over medium heat and fry the patties for 2 to 3 minutes on each side until golden. Serve hot or at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "text": "For the dipping sauce, mix the rice vinegar, soy sauce, mirin, sesame oil, sweet chilli sauce, grated ginger and a chopped garlic clove, plus chilli if you like."
    }
  ]
